{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Though he reaches</b> — like מעי מפלה (the grave of the drop-off), and it is the grave. The sense is that there is none who stretches out a hand to help him in the grave, and at the time of destruction, which is brokenness, wealth does not avail souls. It is generosity, and the sense: wealth. The master of wealth is called שוע with a holam, as in: לא נכר שוע (no wealth is recognized)."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra opens by reading בעי (Job 30:24) as equivalent to מעי, interpreting it as referring to the grave; the phrase מעי מפלה alludes to a ravine or pit associated with burial."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:06.388032543Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}